  "title": "ISRO Launches First Imaging Satellite in Geo-orbit, India's EOS-05",
  "summary": "ISRO successfully launches its first ever imaging satellite in geostationary orbit, marking a historic milestone for India. The 2,367-kg EOS-05 satellite, the heaviest Earth observation satellite so far, is placed in its intended orbit after a successful sub-geosynchronous transfer, as announced by ISRO.",
  "facts": [
    {
      "statement": "ISRO launched the EOS-05 satellite on Friday, marking its first imaging mission in geostationary orbit.",
      "confidence": 0.95
    },
    {
      "statement": "The satellite weighs over 2,300 kg and is the heaviest Earth observation satellite ever launched by ISRO.",
      "confidence": 0.95
    },
    {
      "statement": "The satellite's orbit matches Earth's rotational speed at 36,000 km altitude.",
      "confidence": 0.95
    },
    {
      "statement": "The launch was successful, with the satellite placed into the intended sub-geosynchronous transfer orbit about 18 minutes after liftoff.",
      "confidence": 0.95
    }
  ],
